  "_hazards_comment": "One record per hazard: what channel it damages through, what a player reads when it does, and the base damage and tick interval a room inherits by naming it. A room may override `hazard_damage`/`hazard_tick_interval` when its instance of the same hazard is worse -- `extreme_heat` runs hotter in the trial's inner sanctum than on the salt flat -- and may scale it with `weather_hazard_multipliers`. The prose used to be keyed by damage channel, which meant two hazards sharing a channel shared a sentence and a hazard's own name never reached a player.",
